now let me clearly explain the process 
after setup of jenkins 
profile> account> timezone> Asia/Kolkata> apply/save
now in git 
timedatectl set-timezone Asia/Kolkata> sudo systenctl restart jenkins
refresh jenkins page and login
jenkins home> configure> triggers> poll scm > select the pattern ( cron schedule)

now im integrating jenkins with github sutomatically using poll scm
the uses of poll scm is we can schedule the builds in jenkins by setting the time which are represented by 5 stars * * * * *
the 1st *- minutes we can use it like */5 means every 5th minute or just a star is every minute it is applicable to every star in poll scm 

2nd * means hour 
3rd * means date
4th * means month
5th * means day of the week
to be clear 
sunday - 0
mon - 1
tue - 2
wed - 3
thur - 4
fri - 5
sat - 6

for example i want to trigger a build at 01:45 pm on 23rd Novemeber which is sunday
the cron schedule would be like this ""45 13 23 11 0""

or i need to trigger a build for every 2 mins at 1pm on the same day
the cron schedule would be like this "" */2 13 23 11 0 ""

